LANDING PR for story #288, slice B (split the engine: execute_sequence moves to engine/sequence.rs, one function per step form, settled by StepVerdict).

The branch story-288b-execute-sequence is on main 47b0d89b (#403, #429, #288 slice C and #362 are in) and ends at 673c40a0, one commit. It comes from implement-story-288-split-the-en-4fea9976, which shipped (chief: residual, low, no security residual). rebase-and-finish-story-288-slic-ab26b835 (residual, low) rebased it onto #403. It ported the five #403 hunks inside the old execute_sequence into sequence.rs:
- `unproven` became a StepRun field;
- single_step sets Unproven::seat(&report), and SpawnFailed sets Proven;
- tailed_outcome matches report.settled_outcome();
- panel_step sets Unproven::panel(&reports) before panel_outcome consumes them;
- dialect_step passes &mut unproven to dialect_attempt_outcome;
- the step-indeterminate payload carries #403's evidence.
#403's changes outside execute_sequence stay in engine.rs. The controller's exact-coverage gate is green at 673c40a0.

What it delivers:
- execute_sequence (CC 50, 385 lines) leaves crates/brokkr-runtime/src/engine.rs for engine/sequence.rs as sequence_step (CC 12) plus one function per form (single_step, panel_step, dialect_step) and the settling stages in their old order (step_result, between_steps, carry_change, then finish_sequence or checkpoint_step);
- StepVerdict<T> { Goes(T), Ended }, matched exhaustively, not a trait object (decision 0071 ruling 2);
- SequenceRun and Carried as parameter objects (ruling 10), with the seven-argument signature kept, so no test call site moves;
- engine.rs from 4010 to 3570 lines, summed CC from 466 to 416;
- two suppressions removed (quality/suppressions.txt: production excessive_nesting 15 to 14, too_many_lines 37 to 36).

Judge:
1. That it is a move that keeps behaviour and bytes, #403's settlement included: every #403 hunk that was inside the old execute_sequence lives on in sequence.rs with the same semantics, and engine/cleanup_tests.rs passes unchanged. Every journal site keeps its event type, its payload and its order. Ended is returned wherever a terminal event is journaled, so no later step can run after one. The effect/failed payload and the effect/indeterminate reason are the bytes all four old sites wrote. The dialect needs-change early return leaves the armed gate head as it was.
2. That no test file changed, and every test keeps its name and assertions.
3. That the ratchets hold (files, clones, suppressions), that every new function is within CC 15 and 100 lines, and that the stated mutations (Ended made a no-op; ends_sequence's !later_can_emit negated) fail the named tests.

This run lands one pull request under decision 0051 so the contribution gate can vouch for it. If a finding returns the branch, fix exactly that finding and prove it with a test bound by a compiling mutation. Then run cargo fmt --all -- --check, cargo clippy on the crates you touched with -D warnings, typos --hidden, and quality/ratchet.sh files and clones (all clean). Commit one signed-off commit ending "Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>", and never push. Do not run scripts/coverage-exact.sh; the controller runs it.

Threat model (operator ruling, 2026-09-26): catch realistic accidental misuse, and fail closed on what cannot be read.
